---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';

// Static list of starter articles per the content roadmap.
// Add new entries here as you publish real, human-reviewed posts.
const posts = [
  { title: 'How Much Does a Haircut Usually Cost?', href: '/tools/salon-cost-calculator/', desc: 'A breakdown of what drives salon pricing, with a free calculator.', image: '/images/gallery/gallery-salon-reception.jpg' },
  { title: 'How to Choose a Haircut for Your Face Shape', href: '/hairstyles/by-face-shape/', desc: 'General guidance by face shape to bring into your consultation.', image: '/images/gallery/gallery-blonde-waves-2.jpg' },
  { title: 'How Fast Does Hair Grow?', href: '/tools/hair-length-calculator/', desc: 'Average growth rates and how to estimate your own timeline.', image: '/images/gallery/gallery-blonde-waves-1.jpg' },
  { title: 'Questions to Ask Your Hairstylist', href: '/sola-hair-salon/', desc: 'A checklist for your next consultation, especially at an independent studio.', image: '/images/gallery/gallery-private-studio-1.jpg' },
  { title: 'Hair Care Basics for Beginners', href: '/hair-care/', desc: 'Start-from-zero guidance for building a simple, effective routine.', image: '/images/gallery/gallery-esthetics-room-1.jpg' },
  { title: 'What Is a Sola Salon Studio?', href: '/sola-salon-studio/', desc: 'How the salon-suite model works and how to evaluate a professional.', image: '/images/gallery/gallery-private-studio-2.jpg' },
];
---
<Layout
  title="Blog | Hair, Salon & Styling Guides"
  description="Original guides on hair care, salon services, pricing and styling."
  canonicalPath="/blog/"
>
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14">
    <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mb-2"><a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a> / Blog</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Blog</h1>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-4 max-w-2xl">Original guides on hair care, salon services, pricing and styling.</p>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-8 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      Everything here is written specifically for this site — no scraped or
      spun content, no copied articles. Each guide is meant to answer one
      question completely rather than pad out a topic with filler, and each is
      reviewed and updated as the underlying information changes. Below is a
      running list of what's published so far, organized loosely around the
      questions people most often bring into a salon consultation: what
      something costs, how to choose a style, how long hair takes to grow, and
      how to build a hair care routine that actually works for your hair type.
      New guides are added regularly as the site grows — if there's a topic
      you'd like covered, our <a href="/contact/" class="text-rose-600 underline">contact page</a>
      is the fastest way to send a suggestion.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-8 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      We deliberately keep this list to genuinely useful, complete guides rather
      than churning out a large volume of thin posts. If a topic doesn't warrant
      its own full guide yet, it's usually folded into a related page instead of
      published as a half-finished stub. As the site grows, expect this page to
      fill in with more specific, narrower guides alongside the broader ones
      already here — things like individual product breakdowns, deeper dives into
      specific coloring techniques, and seasonal hair care advice.
    </p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      {posts.map((p) => (
        <Card title={p.title} description={p.desc} href={p.href} image={p.image} imageAlt={p.title} />
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-3">How Articles Get Chosen</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Most of what's published here starts from a genuinely common question —
      the kind of thing people search for right before or right after a salon
      appointment. We try to prioritize topics where existing information online
      is either thin, outdated, or written primarily to rank in search results
      rather than to actually help the reader. If a good, thorough answer
      already exists elsewhere, we're less likely to duplicate it just to have
      more pages on the site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Corrections and Updates</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Hair services, pricing norms, and product categories all shift over time,
      so older guides are periodically reviewed and updated rather than left
      static once published. If you notice something that seems outdated or
      incorrect, the fastest way to get it fixed is through our
      <a href="/contact/" class="text-rose-600 underline">contact page</a> — corrections
      are one of the most useful things a reader can send us.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">What to Expect Next</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      New guides go up regularly, generally following the same pattern as the
      site's other content: original writing, human review, and a focus on
      genuinely answering the question rather than padding for length. If a
      topic here interests you but feels incomplete, check back — it's likely
      to get a fuller standalone treatment as the blog grows.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">No Sponsored Rankings</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      The order articles appear in reflects publish date and relevance, not
      payment. We don't accept placement fees to feature a product, technique,
      or service more prominently than the facts warrant, and any future
      sponsored content will be clearly labeled as such rather than blended in
      with our regular editorial guides.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Reading These Alongside the Free Tools</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Several of these guides pair naturally with our
      <a href="/tools/salon-cost-calculator/" class="text-rose-600 underline">Salon Cost Calculator</a>
      and <a href="/tools/hair-length-calculator/" class="text-rose-600 underline">Hair Length Calculator</a> —
      read the relevant guide first for context, then use the calculator to put
      a rough number or timeline on the plan you've settled on.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Written for Readers, Not Search Engines</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      It's worth repeating: nothing here is written primarily to rank for a
      keyword. Every post exists because it answers a real, specific question
      thoroughly. If an article ever feels padded or vague, that's a sign
      something has gone wrong, and it's exactly the kind of thing worth
      flagging through our contact page so it can be fixed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Suggest a Topic</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Have a question this blog hasn't answered yet? That's usually the
      strongest signal for what to write next. Send it through our
      <a href="/contact/" class="text-rose-600 underline">contact page</a> and it may
      show up as a full guide in a future update.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
